      <!-- Detailed Review: Placester -->
      <div id="placester" style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:64px;">
        <h3 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">Placester</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          Placester has been building real estate websites since 2010 and it is the rare vendor in this category that publishes a straight rate card and lets you buy without a demo. Agent Essential is $59 a month or $566 a year, Agent Plus is $79 a month or $758 a year, Agent Premier is $129 a month or $1,238 a year, and team and brokerage tiers run $199, $399 and $599 a month. Annual billing takes 20 percent off, there is no contract, there is a 14 day free trial that does not ask for a credit card, hosting and bandwidth are unlimited and included, and teams are not charged per agent, only for agents who actually launch a website. Support is the thing its customers write about most, and it shows: Placester's own reviews page quotes customers saying "Never had this kind of support from other websites" and "Changes requested were made within half an hour." It reports 4.9 out of 5 across more than 1,800 Google reviews, and it says more than 25,000 businesses use it.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          The product is a genuine real estate website, not a generic builder with an IDX plugin bolted on. Listings, quick search, saved searches and alerts, area and community pages, home valuation pages, custom landing pages, open house and mortgage calculator modules, lead capture popups and forms, email marketing with lead scoring, a CRM that deepens by tier, and integrations with Follow Up Boss, Cloze, Rechat and hundreds more through Zapier. Since 2026 every plan also carries AI tools: an AI Website Builder and Editor, an AI Content Assistant, an AI ready SEO foundation and an automatically generated llms.txt file, which is a more modern setup than most of its competitors. If you want a professional real estate site with live property search, this is one of the cheapest credible ways to get one.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          Now the limits, and there are three that matter. First, the AI is for the website, not for your leads. Every dollar of "built-in AI" here writes and edits pages and content; nothing in the product answers a phone call, and nothing holds a WhatsApp conversation. A lead that fills in a form at 9pm is captured, stored and emailed to you, and then sits there. Second, IDX is not included in the headline number. The Placester IDX Support Fee is $25 a month for every approved MLS contract on every plan, and your local MLS access fee is separate from that again, so the "$59 a month" website is realistically about $84 a month before setup, and a two MLS agent is closer to $109. Add a $300 Professional setup and an Agent Essential plan with one MLS, and year one is about $1,308 on monthly billing or $1,166 on annual billing. Third, you are renting the site. It lives on Placester's managed hosting, so it exists for as long as the subscription does, and Placester says plainly that the subscription cost is not refundable.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          On reputation, the honest picture is more mixed than the Google rating suggests. The Google score is very strong at 4.9 out of 5 from more than 1,800 reviews, and those reviews are overwhelmingly about fast, human support. The other platforms tell a different story: G2 rates Placester 3.5 out of 5 across 84 reviews, the lowest score in a six tool roundup published in 2026, and Trustpilot holds just two reviews in total, both old and both negative, with Trustpilot noting the company has not invited customers so its sample may not be representative. In the same 2026 roundup, a reviewer testing the platform hands-on found that "The AI website builder looped for more than 30 minutes during testing and never produced a finished draft, despite Placester's own marketing promising minutes, not days." That is one person's test rather than a pattern, but it is worth knowing that the AI builder is not always the five minute experience the marketing implies. None of this makes Placester a bad product. It makes it a website platform, bought for a website problem, and that is exactly how it should be judged.
        </p>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <div>
            <p style="color:white;font-weight:600;font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:8px;">Pros</p>
            <ul style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;">
              <li>Lowest published entry price among real estate specific builders ($59/mo)</li>
              <li>Full rate card published, no demo required to see the price</li>
              <li>Genuine real estate IDX website with live listing search and alerts</li>
              <li>No contract, cancel any time, 14 day free trial with no credit card</li>
              <li>20 percent off on annual billing, first year about $866 with one MLS</li>
              <li>Unlimited hosting and bandwidth included, no per-agent fee for teams</li>
              <li>Built-in AI for site building, content and an auto generated llms.txt</li>
              <li>Integrations with Follow Up Boss, Cloze, Rechat and Zapier</li>
              <li>Support is genuinely its strongest reviewed attribute</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p style="color:white;font-weight:600;font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:8px;">Cons</p>
            <ul style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;">
              <li>Its AI is for the website, not for answering your leads</li>
              <li>Does not answer a phone call or hold a WhatsApp conversation</li>
              <li>IDX costs $25/month per active MLS contract on top of the plan</li>
              <li>Your MLS access fee is charged separately again</li>
              <li>DIY by default, setup is $300 / $500 / $1,200 and editing is $75/mo</li>
