      <div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--bs-bg-raised),var(--bs-bg-raised));border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:64px;border:1px solid rgba(255,45,149,0.3);">
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">🏆 The Bottom Line</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          This is not a fight BirkyStudio wins on websites, and we are not going to pretend it is. <strong style="color:white;">Placester is a genuinely good, genuinely cheap real estate website platform.</strong> It publishes its prices, starts at $59 a month, has no contract, gives a 14 day free trial without a credit card, connects to your MLS, throws in AI for building and editing the site, and reports 4.9 out of 5 across more than 1,800 Google reviews. If your problem is that you do not have a professional IDX website, it solves that for less than almost anyone else, and we would tell you to buy it.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          But be clear about what it is not, because the marketing blurs this. Placester's AI is AI for the website, not AI for your leads. It does not answer a phone call, it does not hold a WhatsApp conversation, and a lead arriving at 9pm is captured and stored rather than spoken to. IDX is charged on top at $25 a month per active MLS contract, and your MLS access fee is separate again, so the real entry cost is closer to $84 a month before setup. The site is hosted and managed by the platform, the subscription is not refundable, and the pages exist only as long as the payments do. The ratings split too: excellent on Google, 3.5 out of 5 on G2 across 84 reviews, and only two old reviews on Trustpilot. <strong style="color:white;">BirkyStudio is a different purchase.</strong> You are not renting a website builder, you are buying the front desk. The AI answers your phone and WhatsApp 24/7 in two languages, follows up automatically, and hands you verified prospects you own, on a website whose code is yours and whose pages stay live whether or not we ever speak again.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:24px;">
          The cleanest way to see it: Placester is the cheapest way to own a real estate website, and BirkyStudio is the cheapest way to stop losing leads who call when you are busy. If you only have one budget, buy the one that matches the problem you actually have. If you have both problems, they stack neatly, Placester for the IDX site and BirkyStudio for the conversation that happens when the lead calls.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose Placester if:</strong> you want a real estate specific IDX website from $59 a month, you are happy to build and edit it yourself, and your leads are already reaching you fast enough.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose BirkyStudio if:</strong> you want the phone and the WhatsApp answered 24/7 in two languages, automatic follow-up, verified prospects you own and a website that stays yours, without a monthly platform fee.
        </p>
