            Explore Placester →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ -->
      <h2 id="faq" style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div style="margin-bottom:48px;">

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>How much does Placester cost?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            Placester publishes its prices, and they are the lowest entry point among real estate specific website builders. Agent plans are Agent Essential at $59 a month or $566 billed annually, Agent Plus at $79 a month or $758 annually, and Agent Premier at $129 a month or $1,238 annually. Team and brokerage plans are Team at $199 a month, Broker Standard at $399 a month and Broker Plus at $599 a month. IDX is charged separately at $25 a month per active MLS contract on every plan, and your local MLS access fee is separate again. Setup services are $300 for Professional, $500 for Semi-Custom or $1,200 for Custom, each one-time, with additional creative hours at $40 to $50 each. Add-ons include an extra website at $25 a month, Content Automation from $15 a month and the Do It For Me editing service from $75 a month. A solo agent on Agent Essential with one IDX connection pays about $866 in year one on annual billing, or $1,008 on monthly billing.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Does Placester answer my phone or reply on WhatsApp?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            No. Placester is a website and IDX platform. It builds you a real estate site, connects it to your MLS so buyers can search listings, and captures leads through forms, popups, landing pages, home valuation pages and live chat. It does not pick up an inbound phone call and it does not hold a WhatsApp conversation. When a lead comes in at 9pm, Placester stores it and can email you about it, and then the lead waits until you are free. BirkyStudio's Voice Receptionist is $550 one-time plus Vapi usage of about $30 to $50 a month and answers calls 24/7 in English and Spanish, and the WhatsApp Text Receptionist is $297 one-time.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Is Placester's AI a receptionist or a website builder?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            It is a website builder. Every Placester plan now includes AI Website Builder and Editor, an AI Content Assistant, an AI ready SEO foundation and an automatically generated llms.txt file. That AI writes and edits the site, generates marketing content, landing pages and area guides, and gets the pages ready for Google and AI search. It is a genuinely useful set of tools for building a site fast, and it is not a voice agent. Placester's AI does not talk to your leads, does not answer a call and does not hold a conversation. BirkyStudio's AI is the opposite: The Base Agent is $1,297 solo with the Notion CRM included and answers and follows up with every enquiry automatically, and the AI Receptionist covers the phone and WhatsApp.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Do I own my website if I build it on Placester?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            You own your domain and your content, and you do not own the platform the site runs on. Placester includes secure unlimited hosting and bandwidth on all plans, so the site lives inside a rented, managed environment rather than on infrastructure you hold. Placester is explicit that you can cancel at any time, that a monthly plan ends on your last billing day and that an annual plan runs until the paid portion is used up, and that the subscription cost is not refundable. So the practical answer is that the pages, the templates and the search experience belong to the platform, and the site stops when the subscription does. BirkyStudio builds the website on your own account for $499 for a 1 to 3 page Starter site, $999 for a Professional 4 to 7 page bilingual site or $1,999 for a Premium 10+ page site with a blog, and you own the code.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Does Placester include IDX, and is it extra?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            Placester is built around IDX and it is charged on top of the plan, not included. The Placester IDX Support Fee is $25 a month for every approved MLS contract on every plan, and your local MLS access fee is separate from that again, so a two MLS agent pays $50 a month before the plan fee is counted. Agent Essential covers a single MLS integration and Agent Plus and above cover unlimited MLS integrations, both at the same $25 a month per IDX. That brings the real monthly cost of an IDX website to about $84 to $154 depending on tier, or $866 in year one on Agent Essential with one MLS connection. BirkyStudio does not include an MLS feed or IDX property search at all, and we say so plainly instead of pretending it does.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Is BirkyStudio cheaper than Placester?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            No, and this is the part where Placester wins. If all you need is a real estate IDX website and you are willing to build and edit it yourself, Placester is cheaper: Agent Essential with one IDX connection is about $866 in year one on annual billing, and about $3,024 over three years on monthly billing. BirkyStudio charges more because it does more. The Base Agent is $1,297 one-time with the Notion CRM included, and with optional care at $97 a month that is about $2,461 in year one and about $4,789 over three years. The difference buys two things Placester does not sell: something that answers your phone and WhatsApp 24/7 in two languages, and a verified, enriched, scored prospect list you own ($497 Starter or $997 Pro, one-time). If you do not need those, buy Placester and keep the difference.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Does Placester have a contract or a free trial?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            Placester is unusually clean on both counts, and it is genuinely better than most of its competitors here. There are no contracts, you can cancel any time, and there is a 14 day free trial that does not require a credit card, with the pricing page also noting up to 21 days of trial access. Annual billing takes 20 percent off and a monthly plan simply ends on your last billing day, while an annual plan continues until the paid portion runs out. The one catch is that the subscription cost is not refundable. BirkyStudio is also contract free: there is no minimum term, no per-seat fee, no cancellation fee, and there is a 30 day money back guarantee on the build itself.
          </div>
        </details>

      </div>

